{"message": "Heads-up before I finalize ACIA-POL-2026-117, plus one question.

Flag: the 2 Oct staff summary says GAAIA is "not yet formally introduced," but the frontier-governance core of the draft was introduced 23 July 2026 as H.R. 9925, the FRONTIER Act (Obernolte/Trahan; referred to E&C and Science, Space, and Technology). The sponsors' broader 269-page GAAIA discussion draft itself has not been introduced, and Trahan's office confirmed in June the comment channel (GAAIA@mail.house.gov) is open, so the work order still works as written.

Question: want me to cross-reference H.R. 9925 in the comment letter (e.g., "our comments on Secs. 111-112 apply equally to the FRONTIER Act")? I think it makes us look current, but I'll keep it strictly to the discussion draft if you prefer. I've confirmed section numbers against the sponsors' section-by-section (Sec. 102 CAISI, Sec. 111 transparency/incident reporting, Sec. 112 IVO audits, Sec. 121 preemption/3-year sunset). Proceeding on the draft now; will adjust if you want changes."}
